{
  "info": {
    "name": "RobinKeyz — Auth",
    "description": "Login, profile and the forget-password flow.\n\n### Setup\nSelect the **RobinKeyz — Local** environment before sending anything. All tokens are stored there, which is why the User collection can reuse them.\n\n### Tokens are set automatically\n| Request | Writes |\n|---|---|\n| Login | `accessToken` |\n| Forget Password | `forgotToken` |\n| Resend OTP | `forgotToken` |\n| Verify Forget OTP | `resetToken` |\n\nYou never paste a token by hand. The only manual step is the OTP, which arrives by email.\n\n### Forget-password order\nForget Password → (read OTP from email) → Verify Forget OTP → Reset Password",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}", "type": "string" }]
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Login",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "",
              "pm.test('Token is returned', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.data).to.have.property('token');",
              "});",
              "",
              "pm.test('Password is not exposed', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(body.data.user).to.not.have.property('password');",
              "});",
              "",
              "// Saved to the environment so the User collection can use it too.",
              "if (body.data && body.data.token) {",
              "  pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.data.token);",
              "  console.log('accessToken saved:', body.data.token.slice(0, 25) + '...');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{loginEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{loginPassword}}\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/login",
          "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "login"]
        },
        "description": "Logs in and **saves `accessToken` to the environment automatically**.\n\nChange `loginEmail` / `loginPassword` in the environment to log in as someone else.\n\n| Field | Required |\n|---|---|\n| `email` | yes |\n| `password` | yes |\n| `isRememberMe` | no — `true` gives a 30 day token instead of `JWT_EXPIRES_IN` |\n\n**Expected:** 200 with `data.token` and `data.user`."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Login — Remember Me",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "if (body.data && body.data.token) {",
              "  pm.environment.set('accessToken', body.data.token);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{loginEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{loginPassword}}\",\n  \"isRememberMe\": true\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/login",
          "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "login"]
        },
        "description": "Same as Login, but the token lasts 30 days.\n\nPaste the token into [jwt.io](https://jwt.io) and compare `exp` with the normal login to see the difference."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Login — Wrong Password (401)",
      "request": {
        "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{loginEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"definitely-wrong\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/login",
          "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "login"]
        },
        "description": "**Expected:** 401 — `Invalid credentials`.\n\nAn email that does not exist returns the exact same message, on purpose: a different message would let an attacker discover which emails are registered."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Get Me",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test('Password is not exposed', () => {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().data).to.not.have.property('password');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/me",
          "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "me"]
        },
        "description": "Returns the logged-in user. Uses `{{accessToken}}` from the environment.\n\n**Expected:** 200. Without a token: 401 — `No token provided or invalid format.`"
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Forget Password — send OTP",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "if (body.data && body.data.token) {",
              "  pm.environment.set('forgotToken', body.data.token);",
              "  console.log('forgotToken saved. Now read the OTP from your email.');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "auth": { "type": "noauth" },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{loginEmail}}\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/forget-password",
          "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "forget-password"]
        },
        "description": "Step 1 of 3.\n\nStores a 6 digit OTP valid for 10 minutes and emails it. **Saves `forgotToken` to the environment automatically.**\n\nThe returned token carries `purpose: \"forgot\"` and cannot be used to reset a password directly.\n\n**Expected:** 200. Unknown email: 404 — `This account does not exist.`"
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Verify Forget OTP",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "if (body.data && body.data.token) {",
              "  pm.environment.set('resetToken', body.data.token);",
              "  console.log('resetToken saved. You can now send Reset Password.');",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            { "key": "token", "value": "{{forgotToken}}", "type": "string" }
          ]
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"otp\": \"{{otp}}\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/verify-forget-otp",
          "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "verify-forget-otp"]
        },
        "description": "Step 2 of 3. Sends `forgotToken`, not `accessToken`.\n\n**Set the `otp` environment variable to the code from your email first**, or type the digits into the body directly.\n\nOn success the OTP row is deleted, so the same code cannot be used twice. **Saves `resetToken` automatically.**\n\n**Expected:** 200.\n\n| Case | Result |\n|---|---|\n| Wrong code | 400 — `Wrong OTP` |\n| Older than 10 minutes | 400 — `OTP has expired` |\n| Already used | 404 — `OTP not found!` |"
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Resend OTP",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('Status is 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "",
              "const body = pm.response.json();",
              "if (body.data && body.data.token) {",
              "  pm.environment.set('forgotToken', body.data.token);",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            { "key": "token", "value": "{{forgotToken}}", "type": "string" }
          ]
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/resend-otp",
          "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "resend-otp"]
        },
        "description": "Optional step. Replaces the stored OTP with a new one and emails it again. Needs `forgotToken`.\n\nThe previous code stops working. **Refreshes `forgotToken` automatically.**\n\n**Expected:** 200."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Reset Password",
      "request": {
        "auth": {
          "type": "bearer",
          "bearer": [
            { "key": "token", "value": "{{resetToken}}", "type": "string" }
          ]
        },
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"password\": \"newpass123\",\n  \"confirmPassword\": \"newpass123\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/reset-password",
          "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "reset-password"]
        },
        "description": "Step 3 of 3. Sends `resetToken`, not `forgotToken`.\n\nSending `forgotToken` here returns **401 — `Invalid token`**, because each token is scoped to one step. Worth trying once to see it work.\n\n| Field | Rule |\n|---|---|\n| `password` | at least 6 characters |\n| `confirmPassword` | must match |\n\n**Expected:** 200.\n\nAfterwards update `loginPassword` in the environment, or Login will start failing."
      },
      "response": []
    },
    {
      "name": "Change Password",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"oldPassword\": \"{{loginPassword}}\",\n  \"newPassword\": \"final1234\",\n  \"confirmPassword\": \"final1234\"\n}",
          "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } }
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{apiUrl}}/auth/change-password",
          "host": ["{{apiUrl}}"],
          "path": ["auth", "change-password"]
        },
        "description": "For a logged-in user. No OTP involved — uses `accessToken`.\n\n**Expected:** 200.\n\n| Case | Result |\n|---|---|\n| No token | 401 |\n| Wrong `oldPassword` | 400 — `Old password is incorrect.` |\n| `confirmPassword` differs | 400 |\n| New same as old | 400 |\n\nAfterwards update `loginPassword` in the environment."
      },
      "response": []
    }
  ]
}
